  "id": "parallelism",
  "term": "parallelism",
  "definition": "In historical psychology, parallelism is the view that mental and bodily events run alongside each other as two aspects of one underlying reality. It holds that mind and body are not reduced to each other and do not causally act on one another, but occur in corresponding sequence.",
